    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.33545/2618060x.2026.v9.i4sb.5372",
    "abstract": "Pigeon pea farming in the rainfed agro-ecosystems of Southern Odisha is highly susceptible to climate fluctuations, especially unpredictable rainfall, droughts, and persistent cloud cover during key growth phases. This research combines long-term climate data, farmer insights, Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (FMEA), and Machine Learning (ML) to evaluate risks and identify mitigation options. Rainfall data (1994-2023) showed concentrated monsoon rainfall, with frequent rains over 200 mm from July to September, aligning with flowering and pod formation. Satellite data indicated over 80% cloudy days during this period, diminishing solar radiation and impacting yields. Farmers reported yield reductions of 10% to 50%, with Rayagada experiencing greater vulnerability. FMEA pinpointed major risks such as unfilled pods, pests, moisture stress, and late sowing, linked to rainfall variability and cloudiness. The ML model achieved high accuracy (R\u00b2=0.982, RMSE=11.41 kg/ha), effectively predicting site-specific yield changes. Simulating a 15-day shorter crop cycle revealed that medium-duration varieties could sustain or boost yields, unlike traditional types which declined. Implementing seedling transplanting alongside ML-based yield prediction offers a promising method to reduce climate risks and improve resilience in rainfed pigeon pea systems. These insights support proactive, localized strategies from optimized sowing times to pest management with bio-inputs that promote climate-smart pigeon pea cultivation. By integrating empirical risk analysis with advanced predictive tools, this FMEA-ML framework provides a scalable model to protect smallholder farmers\u2019 yields amid growing climate challenges, fostering sustainable agriculture across rainfed regions in South Asia.",
    "field": "Climate-smart agriculture",
    "problem": "Existing research addresses risks to pigeon pea production in isolation, lacking an integrated framework that systematically assesses interconnected threats like rainfall variability and cloud cover, thereby failing to provide holistic, predictive mitigation strategies for vulnerable rainfed farming systems.",
    "method": "The paper proposes an integrated framework combining Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (FMEA) and Machine Learning (ML) to assess risks and design localized mitigation strategies for climate-vulnerable pigeon pea production in rainfed agro-ecosystems.",
    "task": "The task is to assess risks in rainfed pigeon pea production using a combined Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (FMEA) and Machine Learning (ML) approach to design localized mitigation strategies for smallholder farmers.",
    "model": [
        "DSSAT",
        "APSIM"
    ],
