            "paragraph": "The Moderate Resolution Imaging Spectroradiometer (MODIS), onboard NASA's Terra and Aqua satellites, captures data across multiple spectral bands that are essential for detecting and analyzing cloud cover in daily satellite imagery. Key bands used for cloud identification include those in the visible spectrum (e.g., Band 1: 620-670 nm), near-infrared (e.g., Band 2: 841-876 nm), shortwave infrared (e.g., Band 6: 1628-1652 nm), and thermal infrared (e.g., Band 31: 10.78-11.28 \u00b5m). These bands are used in various cloud detection algorithms, including thresholding, reflectance-ratio tests, and brightness-temperature assessments, to differentiate clouds from clear-sky pixels and to determine cloud properties such as phase, temperature, and optical thickness. In the present study, MODIS daily surface reflectance data (MODIS/061/MOD09GA) were utilized to extract cloud cover information at the village level.",
